  "observations": [
    "All21 CookVIII26-27 prompts retain exact original controls;26.6 wǣstm original is governed separately by C01. 87.d is bareðe, directly illustrated onFB52;87.b is the compound strategy.",
    "The source159-word opening argument runs156.1-158.4. It is a complete thesis/examples/conclusion unit; the next luxury/death argument is unassigned.",
    "Cook81-87 separately lists differing prefix meanings and warns that compound constituents do not mechanically yield an idiomatic whole-word translation. Attested family analysis is bounded accordingly.",
    "C04:27.4wund43 is inapplicable to feminine wound noun, confirmed BT1281a and exact Luke16.21 quotation atSupplement570b. Cook43 is masculine;51b gives the appropriate feminine model.",
    "C05:157n1 retains pointer156n12, which concerns torrum/crag. The relevant rest-of comparison is156n11. Keep original pointer and separate supplied interpretation.",
    "400dpi reinspection confirms dūst at283 and gōd-wębb at296. Provisional unmarked vowels were audit transcription errors, not source variants or corrections to Cook.",
    "Cook94 explicitly supplies dative pity gemiltsa mē and dative receiving onfēng ðǣre wununge. Cook100-101 separates dative and accusative reflexive uses; literal source controls remain independently decoded.",
    "Cook303 gives līeg as thunderbolt/levin; final canonical translation uses thunderbolts/lightning, correcting the coordinator and design source-first witnesses which initially used flames.",
    "Cook287, not286, contains feorran at the top of the left column. Locator finding sent to grammar worker before seal.",
    "Actual later register records verify u11-articled-righteous-persons and rihtwis-people for A06, and u12-sendan-recipient for C04. They were not inferred from the narrower earlier general descriptions.",
    "Additional actual image inspection: FB54–55 assigns strong preterite second singular and subjunctive to the plural stem and prints contracted fōn endings; FB60–61 gives s:r strongII alternation, the īe umlaut and s-stem -st contraction; FB64 supplies bæd/bǣdon/beden; FB65 explicitly prints hęfst/hęfð and hōf/hōfon/hafen; FB67 fōn/fēng/fēngon/fangen; FB68 weak dental and gemētan participle-contraction models. These corroborate the selected verbal rules, without claiming this spot check inspected every later paradigm cell."
  ],
